{
  "Identifier": "bb29918c-e156-418b-83f4-f983f2654451",
  "Name": "TAKEONPRODUCTIONPALLET",
  "Description": "Takeon Production Pallet (SAGE ASSEMBLY)\n\nIn Egg Production - Create a Pallet (CarryingEntity), with a Trackingentity on it.  Defaulted Item Code, Location, etc.\nThe LOT Number is a Julian Date derivative.\nThe Reason for Pallet is that 2 lots can be combined at the end of a run..\nThe Label is printed as the Pallet Label using CLR, Not as TrackingEntity\n\nVery good use of TAKEON in Production to Generate a pallet with SAGE Assembly and a Pallet Barcode printed.\nThe LABEL_TRACKINGENTITY and LABEL_PALLET Views are Included.\nThere is a step 201 that also consumes Stock in Production location according to the BOM.  Views for BOM Header and BOM Detail are also included.\nFinally - the CarryingEntity includes a routine for allocating an SSCC number.  This SSCC Column is added to the CarryingEntity Table",
